From 5f820125ff5aadec1f3931b7689b747528d5338e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Coen <coen@graafstal.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:28:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/33] xmem: serve the physical-page exports the retail
 executable reaches at startup

XMemAllocatePhysicalPages, XMemFreePhysicalPages, XMemMapPhysicalPages and
XMemMapPhysicalPagesScatter, with the shapes of the executable's call sites.
A page is a 64 KiB slot of a pagefile-backed section; a 64 KiB-page
reserve-only XMemVirtualAlloc is a placeholder reservation, and mapping a
page replaces its placeholder with a view of the slot, so one page can be
mapped at several addresses as on the console. The title's VirtualFree
releases such a reservation whole.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
